---
import BaseLayout from "@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { siteConfig } from "@/config/site";

const updated = "August 2, 2026";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="Learn how Toolsiva processes information, protects browser-based input and handles third-party services."
>
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-12 sm:px-6 lg:py-16">
    <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-brand-300">Legal</p>
    <h1 class="mt-2 text-3xl font-black tracking-tight text-white sm:text-4xl">Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-zinc-500">Last updated: {updated}</p>

    <div class="prose-premium mt-8 space-y-8 text-sm leading-7 text-zinc-300">
      <section>
        <h2>1. Overview</h2>
        <p>
          Toolsiva provides browser-based utilities for text, developer data, security tasks,
          QR codes, calculations and conversions. We designed the service to minimize collection
          of personal information.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>2. Information processed by tools</h2>
        <p>
          Most tool input is processed locally in your browser. Unless a tool clearly states
          otherwise, the content you enter is not intentionally transmitted to Toolsiva servers.
          Do not enter confidential information unless you have independently verified that the
          tool and your device are appropriate for that use.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>3. Technical information</h2>
        <p>
          Hosting and security providers may automatically process limited technical data such as
          IP address, browser type, device information, requested URL, timestamps and security
          events. This information may be used to deliver the site, prevent abuse and maintain
          reliability.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>4. Cookies, analytics and advertising</h2>
        <p>
          Toolsiva does not currently require an account. If analytics, advertising or other
          non-essential technologies are introduced, this policy and any required consent
          controls will be updated before those technologies are enabled.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>5. Third-party services</h2>
        <p>
          The website may rely on infrastructure, content delivery, security or other service
          providers. Those providers process information under their own terms and privacy
          policies. Toolsiva does not sell personal information.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>6. Data retention</h2>
        <p>
          Browser-processed tool content is not intentionally retained by Toolsiva. Technical
          logs retained by infrastructure providers may be kept for limited operational,
          security and legal purposes.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>7. Children</h2>
        <p>
          Toolsiva is a general-audience service and is not directed to children under the age
          required for independent consent in their jurisdiction.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>8. Your choices</h2>
        <p>
          You may clear browser data, disable optional browser storage and stop using the service.
          Privacy rights vary by location. Requests may be sent to
          <a href={`mailto:${siteConfig.contactEmail}`}>{siteConfig.contactEmail}</a>.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>9. Policy changes</h2>
        <p>
          We may update this policy as the service changes. The latest revision date will appear
          at the top of this page.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
